<title>TURKEY: Turkish fighter crashes, two crew hurt.</title>
<headline>Turkish fighter crashes, two crew hurt.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Turkish fighter aircraft crashed on Tuesday during a training flight in southeast Turkey, the Anatolian news agency said.</p>
<p>It said the two crew were injured after ejecting from the F-4 fighter before it crashed at around 9:45 a.m. (0745 GMT) in Batman province. The cause of the crash was unknown, the agency said.</p>
